\chapter{Introduction}

Biological regeneration is constrained by competing demands: structural
integrity, cell-cycle safety, and multi-domain coordination. The
Sovereign Regenerative Engine addresses these constraints through a
closed-loop architecture that integrates timing control, invariant
enforcement, geometric closure, recursion safety, and sovereign audit
mechanisms.

This thesis formalizes the mathematical foundations, simulation
architecture, and operational logic of the system.

