\chapter{Regeneration Timing Model}

Regeneration is governed by:
\[
T_{\text{reg}} = \tau_0 \cdot f\big(\|\mathcal{E}_{\text{stress}}(x,t)\|\big),
\]
where $\tau_0$ is a baseline refractory period and $f$ is monotonic.

Activation damping:
\[
\sigma_{\text{threshold}} = g\big(\|\mathcal{E}_{\text{stress}}(x,t)\|\big).
\]

% ---------------------------------------------------------
% CHAPTER 4 — CELL-CYCLE INVARIANTS
% ---------------------------------------------------------
\chapter{Cell-Cycle Invariant System}

Define:
\[
\mathcal{I}_{\text{cc}} = F\big(n(x,t), \mathcal{K}_{\text{DNA}}(x,t),
\mathbf{J}_{\text{biochem}}(x,t)\big),
\]
with recursion depth bounded by:
\[
n(x,t) \leq n_{\max}.
\]

% ---------------------------------------------------------
% CHAPTER 5 — TISSUE MANIFOLD CLOSURE
% ---------------------------------------------------------
\chapter{Tissue Manifold Closure}

Tissue geometry is modeled by a metric tensor $g_{ij}(x,t)$.

Closure update:
\[
g_{ij}(t+\Delta t) = g_{ij}(t) +
\lambda_{\text{reg}} \cdot
\big(\Psi_{\text{target}}^{(ij)} - \Psi_{\text{current}}^{(ij)}\big).
\]

Residual error:
\[
\epsilon = \left\| \Psi_{\text{target}}^{(ij)} -
\Psi_{\text{current}}^{(ij)} \right\|.
\]

% ---------------------------------------------------------
% CHAPTER 6 — RECURSION-SAFE MITOSIS
% ---------------------------------------------------------
\chapter{Recursion-Safe Mitosis}

If a lineage attempts:
\[
n(x,t) > n_{\max},
\]
the system clamps recursion and transitions the lineage to terminal
differentiation.

